  "term": "BWS",
  "definition": "BWS stands for the Belonging at Work Scale, a brief one-dimensional measure of work group inclusion that assesses an employee’s feelings of belongingness at work. It was developed for use across varied workplaces and employee groups and has been linked with factors such as mistreatment in the work climate and leaves of absence.",
